WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.179
<v Callum Reid>Morning. Can everyone hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:14.570
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, got you. The heating in the portakabin, honestly—it's either Arctic or tropical. No middle setting.</v>

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:18.760
<v Sarah Okafor>You've still got your coat on, though.</v>

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.329
<v Marcus Hale>Insurance, that is. Don't trust it.</v>

00:00:22.739 --> 00:00:27.989
<v Callum Reid>Like the defending in the football last night. Absolutely no confidence in any of it.</v>

00:00:29.489 --> 00:00:32.289
<v David Whitfield>We doing football analysis or a stand-up, then?</v>

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.140
<v Callum Reid>All right, all right. Tough audience this morning.</v>

00:00:38.869 --> 00:00:41.670
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, was that me crackling? I've changed headsets.</v>

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.700
<v Olumide Adeyemi>You're clear now. Bit loud, if anything.</v>

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:52.280
<v Callum Reid>Right. Priya Raman and Jamie Brennan aren't with us today. Sarah, how was overnight?</v>

00:00:52.659 --> 00:00:58.259
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, so, finished the repair on the pump in the pit last night. That's all sorted.</v>

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:02.899
<v David Whitfield>Lovely. Not the nicest spot to spend your evening.</v>

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:06.579
<v Sarah Okafor>No. Definitely not getting a five-star review.</v>

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.489
<v Callum Reid>Okay, quick round on the bits from yesterday, then today's work.</v>

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:22.340
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Han asked me to pass on where she's got to with the near-miss write-up. She's had a first look, nothing major so far; she's partway through it.</v>

00:01:23.939 --> 00:01:27.439
<v Hannah Price>Cheers. Wasn't sure I'd get this headset working in time.</v>

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:34.390
<v Marcus Hale>And Whitty asked me to say the function test on the HV board is all done.</v>

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:37.629
<v Callum Reid>Good, thanks.</v>

00:01:38.209 --> 00:01:43.109
<v Callum Reid>Mine—the permit to work and isolation for the GT1 fuel valve—that's sorted. All fine.</v>

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:51.040
<v Sarah Okafor>Haley asked me to flag the site visit with the contractor. Can't go ahead because the parts haven't turned up.</v>

00:01:51.689 --> 00:01:52.890
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah. Frustrating, that.</v>

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.560
<v Callum Reid>Right, onto what we need to agree today.</v>

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:04.549
<v Callum Reid>Davey, can you chase the purchase order for the Line 2 Safety Guard Interlock this morning, whenever you get a chance?</v>

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.939
<v David Whitfield>Yeah—just the purchase order you're after, not chasing a delivery date as well?</v>

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:14.240
<v Callum Reid>Just the purchase order, yeah.</v>

00:02:15.319 --> 00:02:19.169
<v David Whitfield>Okay, I'll chase that this morning, whenever I get a chance.</v>

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:22.909
<v Sarah Okafor>This morning's going to disappear quickly, isn't it?</v>

00:02:23.889 --> 00:02:28.090
<v Callum Reid>Usually does. There's the production downtime slot to pin down as well.</v>

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:36.460
<v Callum Reid>I'll schedule downtime for the little water valve on two with production, at half two. Normal priority, that one.</v>

00:02:38.639 --> 00:02:43.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Reidy. Better having an actual slot than trying to squeeze it in.</v>

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:47.300
<v Marcus Hale>The famous five-minute stop that isn't five minutes.</v>

00:02:49.379 --> 00:02:50.780
<v Callum Reid>Exactly. None of that.</v>

00:02:52.710 --> 00:03:02.159
<v David Whitfield>I'll update the risk assessment for work on the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve, due tomorrow at 9:30. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.909
<v Callum Reid>Agreed, Davey. That risk assessment comes first.</v>

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:09.020
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, I'll put that ahead of the other bits.</v>

00:03:09.349 --> 00:03:12.849
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Get the paperwork right before everyone gets carried away, basically.</v>

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:16.219
<v Sarah Okafor>Absolutely. No sense rushing past that.</v>

00:03:16.919 --> 00:03:19.020
<v Callum Reid>Anything else on your side, then?</v>

00:03:21.169 --> 00:03:30.620
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the long belt by 11am. Not an emergency but don't let it slip—that's how I'm treating it.</v>

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:36.300
<v Marcus Hale>The sensors as well, not just pull the jam out and call it good?</v>

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:40.310
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, both. Clear it and check the sensors, by 11am.</v>

00:03:42.449 --> 00:03:47.349
<v Callum Reid>Right, David Whitfield for that one. Your full name's finally appeared properly on Teams.</v>

00:03:49.689 --> 00:03:52.840
<v David Whitfield>Sounds like I'm being called into the head's office.</v>

00:03:54.789 --> 00:03:57.240
<v Hannah Price>Only if he uses your middle name.</v>

00:03:58.129 --> 00:04:01.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Sorry, talking over you—you're happy with that order of work?</v>

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:08.009
<v David Whitfield>Yeah. Risk assessment first, and the belt by 11am. The purchase-order chase fits round those this morning.</v>

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:09.530
<v Callum Reid>Okay, that works.</v>

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:17.490
<v Hannah Price>Only other thing from me: I heard a slight rattle from the counterbalances. Nothing to action yet, just an observation.</v>

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:22.540
<v Marcus Hale>Hard to hear yourself think round there sometimes.</v>

00:04:24.069 --> 00:04:25.819
<v Hannah Price>Mm. It was only slight.</v>

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:30.850
<v Callum Reid>Right. Anything else anyone needs in the room before we break?</v>

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.319
<v Sarah Okafor>Nothing else from me.</v>

00:04:34.959 --> 00:04:38.110
<v Marcus Hale>No, that's me. Back to the portakabin climate lottery.</v>

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.000
<v Olumide Adeyemi>All good here.</v>

00:04:40.759 --> 00:04:43.560
<v Callum Reid>Lovely. Thanks, everyone. Catch you on the floor.</v>

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:45.620
<v David Whitfield>Cheers, all.</v>
